[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Tutorial: Bridging Oracle Integration and Chainlink in Enterprise Blockchain"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Smart contracts on a blockchain are isolated by design; they cannot inherently fetch external data, connect to legacy systems, or execute off-chain computations. To bridge this gap, oracles are utilized. Chainlink is the industry-standard decentralized oracle network, enabling smart contracts to securely interact with real-world data feeds, APIs, and traditional enterprise systems."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Basic understanding of Solidity and smart contract deployment."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Familiarity with Node.js and JavaScript/TypeScript."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A testnet wallet (such as MetaMask) funded with testnet LINK and ETH."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 1: Understanding the Chainlink Architecture"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Chainlink operates through a decentralized network of nodes that fetch data from external APIs, aggregate the results securely, and deliver them to your smart contract on-chain. This decentralized approach eliminates single points of failure and data manipulation risks."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 2: Writing the Consumer Contract"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"To consume Chainlink data feeds, your smart contract must inherit from the Chainlink client libraries and implement interfaces that communicate with the AggregatorV3Interface. Below is an example of a price consumer contract."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"pragma solidity ^0.8.7;

import "@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/interfaces/AggregatorV3Interface.sol";

contract ChainlinkPriceConsumer {
    AggregatorV3Interface internal priceFeed;

    /**
     * Network: Sepolia
     * Aggregator: ETH/USD
     */
    constructor() {
        priceFeed = AggregatorV3Interface(0x694AA1769357215DE4FAC081bf1f309aDC325306);
    }

    function getLatestPrice() public view returns (int) {
        (
            ,
            int price,
            ,
            ,

        ) = priceFeed.latestRoundData();
        return price;
    }
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Step 3: Deploying and Testing"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Deploy your smart contract using Hardhat or Foundry to the Sepolia testnet. Ensure you supply the correct aggregator contract address corresponding to the desired data feed pair."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"const { ethers } = require("hardhat");

async function main() {
    const PriceConsumer = await ethers.getContractFactory("ChainlinkPriceConsumer");
    const priceConsumer = await PriceConsumer.deploy();
    await priceConsumer.deployed();

    console.log("ChainlinkPriceConsumer deployed to:", priceConsumer.address);

    const latestPrice = await priceConsumer.getLatestPrice();
    console.log("Latest ETH/USD Price:", latestPrice.toString());
}

main().catch((error) => {
    console.error(error);
    process.exitCode = 1;
});"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"You have successfully integrated Chainlink oracles into your blockchain application, enabling your smart contracts to dynamically read real-world data feeds securely and reliably."}]
